+## 2026-09-01 — Launcher SPEC 0.1.2-draft: file-kind probe rekeyed on the adapter registry (TASK-260901-25zqel rework 1)
+
+- FINDING (review RUN-260901-7354f1, MAJOR, confirmed): the 0.1.1-draft §5.1 probe keyed on the fragment's `system_prompt.channels` list, so a pi launch whose fragment carried no `system_prompt` section probed nothing while the tool still applied a stray `SYSTEM.md` full-replace — a silent bypass of the §5.2 warning contract. The paragraph asserted Curator drift-and-repair covers the stray file, but environments.md §10.1 repair leaves unmanaged files untouched and §8.4 drift covers only marker-recorded surfaces: the asserted guard never runs on that path.
+- MILESTONE: SPEC.md 0.1.2-draft, signed commit `6de42d8` (verifies G) on `draft/spec-pi-file-channels` atop `0029b36`, base `origin/main` @ `dae0c35`; not pushed. The §5.1 probe is now keyed on the environment adapter's closed file-channel filename set (revision 1: exactly `pi` — `APPEND_SYSTEM.md`, `SYSTEM.md`) and runs on every launch into a managed home, fragment `system_prompt` section or not; a present-and-readable file with no corresponding fragment descriptor is an active channel and triggers the full §5.2 warning set. build/vet exit 0.
+- DECISION: removal ownership stated honestly — a marker-recorded materialized file belongs to Curator's materialization/drift/repair (§5.5/§8.4); any other file at a registry filename is unmanaged, no automated contract removes it, and every launcher-mediated launch warns until the operator removes it. Residuals recorded in §9: hand launches bypass the probe (the launcher is never mandatory), and the pre-exec probe is point-in-time, so a file written between probe and tool startup goes undetected; neither is closable from the launcher's seat.
