+## 2026-09-01 — Launcher SPEC 0.1.1-draft: pi file-kind channel semantics (TASK-260901-25zqel)
+
+- MILESTONE: SPEC.md §5 restructured into §5.1/§5.2 to close the carried review minor on file-kind channels (`pi` `APPEND_SYSTEM.md`/append, `SYSTEM.md`/replace). Launcher never places/removes/edits the files (Curator materialization under the `system_prompt_files` machine setting owns them); mandatory pre-exec presence probe; warning set mandatory for an active file-kind channel even without `--system-prompt`; file-kind presence orthogonal and additive to the flag-class opt-in, warning enumerates every active channel; `sysprompt_file_unreadable` added to §6; §8.1 Revision history added. Signed commit `0029b36` (verifies G) on `draft/spec-pi-file-channels`, base `origin/main` @ `dae0c35`; not pushed. build/vet exit 0.
+- DECISION: an absent file-kind file is the channel's legitimate inactive state, never a diagnostic — the fragment reproduces pi's §7.3 descriptor list unconditionally and `system_prompt_files` defaults to `off`, so treating absence as an error would fail every plain pi launch. `sysprompt_file_unreadable` fires only on a present-but-unreadable or non-regular-file probe, preserving the §6 absence-vs-read-failure invariant. The producer brief's "absent/unreadable" wording was deliberately narrowed to unreadable; rationale recorded in `TASK-260901-25zqel_launcher-pi-channels-notes.md`.
+- DECISION: a `file`-kind descriptor never satisfies the `--system-prompt` opt-in — opt-in selection considers only `flag`/`config-key`/`variable`; matching-semantics file presence does not avert `sysprompt_channel_unavailable`, and the launcher does not arbitrate tool-side precedence when both a flag and a file engage on one launch.
+
