+- DECISION: `--system-prompt` takes a required `append|replace` value — the launcher never defaults to the destructive replace channel, and an opt-in with no matching fragment channel is `sysprompt_channel_unavailable`, not a silent no-op.
+- DECISION: the launcher owns the closed env-id→agentic-system mapping (claude_code→claude-code, codex_cli→codex, pi→pi; opencode `env_unsupported` in revision 1) — it is the only component speaking both vocabularies; neither curator-spec nor agents-management assigns this mapping elsewhere.
+- DECISION: no diagnostic downgrades a launch — `ax_handoff_failed` never falls back to untracked direct exec, and a malformed fragment read is `resolve_fragment_invalid`, never treated as absence. Child env merges process < plan < fragment, fragment winning on exactly its closed adapter-registry names (§10.3 boundary makes that safe).
+- NOTE: `go run` masks the child's exit code as 1; the exit-2 smoke needs the compiled binary.
